Quantification of Loss – Special damages

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > 10. Quantification of Loss – Special damages] 10.1 In all cases, if the defendant admits liability, the claimant will send to the defendant as soon as reasonably practicable a schedule of any past and future expenses and losses which he claims, even if the schedule is necessarily provisional. The schedule should contain as much detail as reasonably practicable and should identify those losses that are ongoing. If the schedule is likely to be updated before the case is concluded, it should say so. The claimant should keep the defendant informed as to the rate at which his financial loss is progressing throughout the entire Protocol period. ## 11. Stocktake

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > 11. Stocktake] 11.1 Where the procedure set out in this Protocol has not resolved the dispute between the parties, each party should undertake a review of its own positions and the strengths and weaknesses of its case. The parties should then together consider the evidence and the arguments in order to see whether litigation can be avoided or, if that is not possible, for the issues between the parties to be narrowed before proceedings are issued. Where the defendant is insured and the pre-action steps have been taken by the insurer, the insurer would normally be expected to nominate solicitors to act in the proceedings and to accept service of the claim form and other documents on behalf of the defendant. The claimant or their solicitor is recommended to invite the insurer to nominate the insurer to nominate solicitors to act in the proceedings and do so 7 to 14 days before the intended issue date. ## Annex A: Illustrative flow chart

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Annex A: Illustrative flow chart] Download Annex A: Illustrative flow chart (PDF, 122 KB)

## Annex B: Templates for letters of claim and response

## B1 Letter of Claim

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] To

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Defendant

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Dear Sirs

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Re:

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Claimant’s full name

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Claimant’s full address

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Claimant’s Clock or Works Number

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Claimant’s Employer (name and address)

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] We are instructed by the above named to claim damages in connection with an accident at work/road traffic accident/tripping accident on day of (year) at (place of accident which must be sufficiently detailed to establish location)

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Please confirm the identity of your insurers. Please note that the insurers will need to see this letter as soon as possible and it may affect your insurance cover and/or the conduct of any subsequent legal proceedings if you do not send this letter to them. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Clear summary of the facts

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] The circumstances of the accident are:

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] (brief outline)

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Liability

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] The reason why we are alleging fault is:

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] (simple explanation e.g. defective machine, broken ground)

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] We are obtaining a police report and will let you have a copy of the same upon your undertaking to meet half the fee. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Injuries

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] A description of our clients’ injuries is as follows:

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] (brief outline) The description should include a non-exhaustive list of the main functional effects on daily living, so that the defendant can begin to assess value / rehabilitation needs. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] (In cases of road traffic accidents)

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Our client (state hospital reference number) received treatment for the injuries at name and address of hospital). [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Our client is still suffering from the effects of his/her injury. We invite you to participate with us in addressing his/her immediate needs by use of rehabilitation. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Loss of Earnings

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] He/She is employed as (occupation) and has had the following time off work (dates of absence) . His/Her approximate weekly income is (insert if known). [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] If you are our client’s employers, please provide us with the usual earnings details which will enable us to calculate his financial loss. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Other Financial Losses

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] We are also aware of the following (likely) financial losses:

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Details of the insurer

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] We have also sent a letter of claim to (name and address) and a copy of that letter is attached. We understand their insurers are (name, address and claims number if known) . [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] At this stage of our enquiries we would expect the documents contained in parts (insert appropriate parts of standard disclosure list) to be relevant to this action. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] A copy of this letter is attached for you to send to your insurers. Finally we expect an acknowledgment of this letter within 21 days by yourselves or your insurers. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B1 Letter of Claim] Yours faithfully

## B2 Letter of response

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] To Claimant’s legal representative

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] Dear Sirs

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] Letter of Response

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] [Claimant’s name] v [Defendant’s name]

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] Parties

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] We have been instructed to act on behalf of [defendant] in relation to your client’s accident on [ ]. We note that you have also written to [defendant] in connection with this claim. We [do/do not] believe they are a relevant party because [ ]. [In addition we believe your claim should be directed against [defendant] for the following reasons:

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] Liability

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] In respect of our client’s liability for this accident we

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] admit the accident occurred and that our client is liable for loss and damage to the claimant the extent of which will require quantification. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] Or

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] admit the accident occurred but deny that our client is responsible for any loss or damage alleged to have been caused for the following reasons:-

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] Or

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > B2 Letter of response] do not admit the accident occurred either in the manner described in your letter of claim [or at all] because:

## Limitation

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] [We do not intend to raise any limitation defence]

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Documents

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] We attach copies of the following documents in support of our client’s position: You have requested copies of the following documents which we are not enclosing as we do not believe they are relevant for the following reasons:

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] [It would assist our investigations if you could supply us with copies of the following documents]

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Next Steps

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] In admitted cases

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Please advise us which medical experts you are proposing to instruct. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Please also supply us with your client’s schedule of past and future expenses [if any] which are claimed, even if this can only be supplied on a provisional basis at present to assist us with making an appropriate reserve. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] If you have identified that the claimant has any immediate need for additional medical treatment or other early rehabilitation intervention so that we can take instructions pursuant to the Rehabilitation Code. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] In non-admitted cases

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Please confirm we may now close our file. Alternatively, if you intend to proceed please advise which experts you are proposing to instruct. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Alternative Dispute Resolution

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Include details of any options that may be considered whether on a without prejudice basis or otherwise. [Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > Limitation] Yours faithfully

## Annex C: Pre-Action Personal Injury Protocol Standard Disclosure Lists

## RTA CASES

## SECTION A

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A] In all cases where liability is at issue–

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A] (i) documents identifying nature, extent and location of damage to defendant’s vehicle where there is any dispute about point of impact;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A] (ii) MOT certificate where relevant;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A] (iii) maintenance records where vehicle defect is alleged or it is alleged by defendant that there was an unforeseen defect which caused or contributed to the accident. ## SECTION B

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION B] Accident involving commercial vehicle as defendant–

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION B] (i) tachograph charts or entry from individual control book;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION B] (ii) maintenance and repair records required for operators’ licence where vehicle defect is alleged or it is alleged by defendant that there was an unforeseen defect which caused or contributed to the accident. ## SECTION C

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C] Cases against local authorities where highway design defect is alleged—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C] (i) documents produced to comply with Section 39 of the Road Traffic Act 1988 in respect of the duty designed to promote road safety to include studies into road accidents in the relevant area and documents relating to measures recommended to prevent accidents in the relevant area;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C] (ii) any Rule 43 reports produced at the request of a coroner pursuant to Schedule 5 of the Coroners & Justice Act 2009, for accidents occurring in the same locus as one covered by an earlier report. ## HIGHWAY TRIPPING CLAIMS

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > HIGHWAY TRIPPING CLAIMS] Documents from Highway Authority for a period of 12 months prior to the accident–

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > HIGHWAY TRIPPING CLAIMS] (i) records of inspection for the relevant stretch of highway;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > HIGHWAY TRIPPING CLAIMS] (ii) maintenance records including records of independent contractors working in relevant area;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > HIGHWAY TRIPPING CLAIMS] (iii) records of the minutes of Highway Authority meetings where maintenance or repair policy has been discussed or decided;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > HIGHWAY TRIPPING CLAIMS] (iv) records of complaints about the state of highways;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > HIGHWAY TRIPPING CLAIMS] (v) records of other accidents which have occurred on the relevant stretch of highway. ## WORKPLACE CLAIMS

## GENERAL DOCUMENTS

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (i) accident book entry;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (ii) other entries in the book or other accident books, relating to accidents or injuries similar to those suffered by our client (and if it is contended there are no such entries please confirm we may have facilities to inspect all accident books);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (iii) first aider report;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (iv) surgery record;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (v) foreman/supervisor accident report;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (vi) safety representative’s accident report;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (vii) RIDDOR (Reporting of Injuries, Diseases and Dangerous Occurrences Regulations) reported to HSE or relevant investigatory agency;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (viii) back to work interview notes and report;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (ix) all personnel/occupational health records relating to our client;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (x) other communications between defendants and HSE or other relevant investigatory agency;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xi) minutes of Health and Safety Committee meeting(s) where accident/matter considered;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xii) copies of all relevant CCTV footage and any other relevant photographs, videos and/or DVDs;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xiii) copies of all electronic communications/documentation relating to the accident;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xiv) earnings information where defendant is employer;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xv) reports to DWP;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xvi) manufacturer’s or dealers instructions or recommendations concerning use of the work equipment;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xvii) service or maintenance records of the work equipment;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xviii) all documents recording arrangements for detecting, removing or cleaning up any articles or substances on the floor of the premises likely to cause a trip or slip;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xix) work sheets and all other documents completed by or on behalf of those responsible for implementing the cleaning policy and recording work done;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xx) all invoices, receipts and other documents relating to the purchase of relevant safety equipment to prevent a repetition of the accident;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxi) all correspondence, memoranda or other documentation received or brought into being concerning the condition or repair of the work equipment/the premises;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxii) all correspondence, instructions, estimates, invoices and other documentation submitted or received concerning repairs, remedial works or other works to the work equipment/the premises since the date of that accident;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxiii) work sheets and all other documents recording work done completed by those responsible for maintaining the work equipment/premises;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxiv) all relevant risk assessments;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxv) all reports, conclusions or recommendations following any enquiry or investigation into the accident;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxvi) the record kept of complaints made by employees together with all other documents recording in any way such complaints or actions taken thereon;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxvii) all other correspondence sent, or received, relating to our client’s injury prior to receipt of this letter of claim;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > GENERAL DOCUMENTS] (xxviii) documents listed above relating to any previous/similar accident/matter identified by the claimant and relied upon as proof of negligence including accident book entries;

## WORKPLACE CLAIMS – DISCLOSURE WHERE SPECIFIC REGULATIONS APPLY

## SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (i) Pre-accident Risk Assessment required by Regulation 3(1);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (ii) Post-accident Re-Assessment required by Regulation 3(2);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (iii) Accident Investigation Report prepared in implementing the requirements of Regulations 4, and 5;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (iv) Health Surveillance Records in appropriate cases required by Regulation 6;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (v) documents relating to the appointment of competent persons to assist required by Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (vi) documents relating to the employees health and safety training required by Regulation 8;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (vii) documents relating to necessary contacts with external services required by Regulation 9;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION A – Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999] (viii) information provided to employees under Regulation 10. ## SECTION B– Workplace (Health Safety and Welfare) Regulations 1992

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION B– Workplace (Health Safety and Welfare) Regulations 1992] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION B– Workplace (Health Safety and Welfare) Regulations 1992] (i) repair and maintenance records required by Regulation 5;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION B– Workplace (Health Safety and Welfare) Regulations 1992] (ii) housekeeping records to comply with the requirements of Regulation 9;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION B– Workplace (Health Safety and Welfare) Regulations 1992] (iii) hazard warning signs or notices to comply with Regulation 17 (Traffic Routes). ## SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (i) manufacturers’ specifications and instructions in respect of relevant work equipment establishing its suitability to comply with Regulation 4;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (ii) maintenance log/maintenance records required to comply with Regulation 5;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (iii) documents providing information and instructions to employees to comply with Regulation 8;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (iv) documents provided to the employee in respect of training for use to comply with Regulation 9;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (v) risk assessments/documents required to comply with Regulation 12;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (vi) any notice, sign or document relied upon as a defence to alleged breaches of Regulations 14 to 18 dealing with controls and control systems;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (vii) instruction/training documents issued to comply with the requirements of Regulation 22 insofar as it deals with maintenance operations where the machinery is not shut down;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (viii) copies of markings required to comply with Regulation 23;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION C – Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998] (ix) copies of warnings required to comply with Regulation 24. ## SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992] (i) documents relating to the assessment of the Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 6;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992] (ii) documents relating to the maintenance and replacement of Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992] (iii) record of maintenance procedures for Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992] (iv) records of tests and examinations of Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992] (v) documents providing information, instruction and training in relation to the Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 9;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION D – Personal Protective Equipment at Work Regulations 1992] (vi) instructions for use of Personal Protective Equipment to include the manufacturers’ instructions to comply with Regulation 10. ## SECTION E – Manual Handling Operations Regulations 1992

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION E – Manual Handling Operations Regulations 1992] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION E – Manual Handling Operations Regulations 1992] (i) Manual Handling Risk Assessment carried out to comply with the requirements of Regulation 4(1)(b)(i);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION E – Manual Handling Operations Regulations 1992] (ii) re-assessment carried out post-accident to comply with requirements of Regulation 4(1)(b)(i);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION E – Manual Handling Operations Regulations 1992] (iii) documents showing the information provided to the employee to give general indications related to the load and precise indications on the weight of the load and the heaviest side of the load if the centre of gravity was not positioned centrally to comply with Regulation 4(1)(b)(iii);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION E – Manual Handling Operations Regulations 1992] (iv) documents relating to training in respect of manual handling operations and training records. ## SECTION F – Health and Safety (Display Screen Equipment) Regulations 1992

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION F – Health and Safety (Display Screen Equipment) Regulations 1992] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION F – Health and Safety (Display Screen Equipment) Regulations 1992] (i) analysis of work stations to assess and reduce risks carried out to comply with the requirements of Regulation 2;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION F – Health and Safety (Display Screen Equipment) Regulations 1992] (ii) re-assessment of analysis of work stations to assess and reduce risks following development of symptoms by the claimant;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION F – Health and Safety (Display Screen Equipment) Regulations 1992] (iii) documents detailing the provision of training including training records to comply with the requirements of Regulation 6;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION F – Health and Safety (Display Screen Equipment) Regulations 1992] (iv) documents providing information to employees to comply with the requirements of Regulation 7. ## SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (i) risk assessment carried out to comply with the requirements of Regulation 6;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (ii) reviewed risk assessment carried out to comply with the requirements of Regulation 6;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (iii) documents recording any changes to the risk assessment required to comply with Regulation 6 and steps taken to meet the requirements of Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (iv) copy labels from containers used for storage handling and disposal of carcinogenics to comply with the requirements of Regulation 7(2A)(h);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (v) warning signs identifying designation of areas and installations which may be contaminated by carcinogenics to comply with the requirements of Regulation 7(2A)(h);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (vi) documents relating to the assessment of the Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7(3A);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (vii) documents relating to the maintenance and replacement of Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7(3A);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (viii) record of maintenance procedures for Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7(3A);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (ix) records of tests and examinations of Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7(3A);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (x) documents providing information, instruction and training in relation to the Personal Protective Equipment to comply with Regulation 7(3A);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xi) instructions for use of Personal Protective Equipment to include the manufacturers’ instructions to comply with Regulation 7(3A);

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xii) air monitoring records for substances assigned a maximum exposure limit or occupational exposure standard to comply with the requirements of Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xiii) maintenance examination and test of control measures records to comply with Regulation 9;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xiv) monitoring records to comply with the requirements of Regulation 10;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xv) health surveillance records to comply with the requirements of Regulation 11;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xvi) documents detailing information, instruction and training including training records for employees to comply with the requirements of Regulation 12;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xvii) all documents relating to arrangements and procedures to deal with accidents, incidents and emergencies required to comply with Regulation 13;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION G – Control of Substances Hazardous to Health Regulations 2002] (xvii) labels and Health and Safety data sheets supplied to the employers to comply with the CHIP Regulations. ## SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (i) notification of a project form (HSE F10) to comply with the requirements of Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (ii) Health and Safety Plan to comply with requirements of Regulation 15;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (iii) Health and Safety file to comply with the requirements of Regulations 12 and 14;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (iv) information and training records provided to comply with the requirements of Regulation 17;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (v) records of advice from and views of persons at work to comply with the requirements of Regulation 18;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (vi) reports of inspections made in accordance with Regulation 33;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (vii) records of checks for the purposes of Regulation 34;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION H – Construction (Design and Management) Regulations 2007] (viii) emergency procedures for the purposes of Regulation 39. ## SECTION I – Construction (Health, Safety & Welfare) Regulations 1996

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION I – Construction (Health, Safety & Welfare) Regulations 1996] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION I – Construction (Health, Safety & Welfare) Regulations 1996] (i) documents produced to comply with requirements of the Regulations. ## SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] Documents including—

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (i) documents relating to planning, supervision and safety carried out for Regulation 4;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (ii) documents relating to training for the purposes of Regulation 5;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (iii) documents relating to the risk assessment carried out for Regulation 6;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (iv) documents relating to the selection of work equipment for the purposes of Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (v) notices or other means in writing warning of fragile surfaces for the purposes of Regulation 9;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (vi) documents relating to any inspection carried out for Regulation 12;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (vii) documents relating to any inspection carried out for Regulation 13;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (viii) reports made for the purposes of Regulation 14;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION J – Work at Height Regulations 2005] (ix) any certificate issued for the purposes of Regulation 15. ## SECTION K – Pressure Systems and Transportable Gas Containers Regulations 1989

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION K – Pressure Systems and Transportable Gas Containers Regulations 1989] (i) information and specimen markings provided to comply with the requirements of Regulation 5;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION K – Pressure Systems and Transportable Gas Containers Regulations 1989] (ii) written statements specifying the safe operating limits of a system to comply with the requirements of Regulation 7;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION K – Pressure Systems and Transportable Gas Containers Regulations 1989] (iii) copy of the written scheme of examination required to comply with the requirements of Regulation 8;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION K – Pressure Systems and Transportable Gas Containers Regulations 1989] (iv) examination records required to comply with the requirements of Regulation 9;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION K – Pressure Systems and Transportable Gas Containers Regulations 1989] (v) instructions provided for the use of operator to comply with Regulation 11;

[Pre-Action Protocol for Personal Injury Claims > SECTION K – Pressure Systems and Transportable Gas Containers Regulations 1989] (vi) records kept to comply with the requirements of Regulation 13;

